{"id":"cf6f6614d5d1560b","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-zfc-card-aleph-function.md","title":"ZFC Card Aleph Function","display":"df-zfc-card-aleph-function — ZFC Card Aleph Function","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-card-aleph-function","aliases":["58-df-zfc-card-aleph-function"],"display":"df-zfc-card-aleph-function — ZFC Card Aleph Function","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-card-aleph-function"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-card-aleph-function</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-card-aleph-function — ZFC Card Aleph Function"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> (class relation in the ambient class metatheory)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ord}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ord}\\)</span> (class of ordinals)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\alpha\">\\(\\aleph_\\alpha\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\">\\(\\alpha\\)</span>-th infinite cardinal, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{AlephFunction}\">\\(\\operatorname{AlephFunction}\\)</span> (class-function predicate defined below)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}card\\text{-}aleph\\text{-}function} \\vdash \\operatorname{AlephFunction}(F)\\leftrightarrow\\forall x\\;\\forall y\\;\\bigl(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in F\\leftrightarrow x\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\land y=\\aleph_x\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}card\\text{-}aleph\\text{-}function} \\vdash \\operatorname{AlephFunction}(F)\\leftrightarrow\\forall x\\;\\forall y\\;\\bigl(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in F\\leftrightarrow x\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\land y=\\aleph_x\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The transfinite recursion, including the limit clause, is supplied by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a>. The displayed formula specifies the graph of a proper-class function; it does not apply the set-function domain operator to a proper class.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md","status":"resolved","id":"535817bf563314f5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md","status":"resolved","id":"535817bf563314f5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\aleph_\\alpha$ ($\\alpha$-th infinite cardinal, see [[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md","status":"resolved","id":"535817bf563314f5","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"The transfinite recursion, including the limit clause, is supplied by [[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]. The displayed formula specifies the graph of a proper-class function; it does not apply the set-function domain operator to a proper class.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Ord}","display":false},{"tex":"\\aleph_\\alpha","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{AlephFunction}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}card\\text{-}aleph\\text{-}function} \\vdash \\operatorname{AlephFunction}(F)\\leftrightarrow\\forall x\\;\\forall y\\;\\bigl(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in F\\leftrightarrow x\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\land y=\\aleph_x\\bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1086,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1477","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-zfc-card-aleph-function.md|58-df-zfc-card-aleph-function]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["535817bf563314f5"]}